  "body": "**Stacked on #1019 (on #1002).** The diff shows their commits until they merge. This PR's own commits are c5e931c6 (posts and tests) and c12b4d16 (conformance synth fixture and goldens).\n\nCloses the two latent seat gaps the high-tier review of #1019 noted (review at 321df394). Neither stream comes from a generator today (the generator always writes the chain plus the rapids that leave it), but a legacy or foreign stream would post an XY traverse lower than the hop.\n\n### What changed (identical in all six canned-cycle mill posts: fanuc, haas, mazak, sinumerik, tormach, doosan-dnm)\n- **Back-to-back cycle records** (`cycleSeat`, the away branch). When the cycle is read away from its hole and no stream rapid took the tool there, the seat now traverses at the section's hop:\n  - `G0(0) Z<max(RetractPlane, R)>` when the tool is below it, then `X Y`, then `Z<R>`;\n  - a tool already above the hop traverses where it stands.\n\n  The hop is the section's own `PARAM RetractPlane`. `onParameter` captures it into `hopZ`, and `onSectionEnd` forgets it, so a section never borrows the previous operation's hop. A section that states no `RetractPlane` is refused by name: \"a canned cycle is read away from its hole with no rapid to it, and the section states no RetractPlane to traverse at\". The seats that stay over the hole (only up or down to R) are unchanged.\n- **Cycle after probing.** `onProbeMove`, `onProbeRetreat` and `onProbeGuard` call a new `probeSeat()`. It sets `seatKnown` the way `chainRapid` / `chainCut` do, and closes an open cycle group with `G80`, because no probe move is part of a hole's chain. The engine already tracks the position through TOUCH / RETREAT / GUARD records, so a cycle read after probing is seated from there.\n- Heidenhain and Carvera post the expanded chain and are untouched; their script suites and goldens are unchanged. fanuc-lathe is not touched (#1025/#1042).\n- `assets/posts/AGENTS.md` (hop law paragraph) and `docs/decisions/1028-cycle-seat-latent.md` record the decisions. `assets/posts/AGENTS.md` is not a process file, so there is no PROCESS_VERSION bump.\n\n### Tests (`crates/post/tests/cycle_hop.rs`, all six posts through the #994 checker)\n- `back_to_back_cycle_records_traverse_at_the_hop`: the recorded `drill_retract` stream with hole 1's hop, traverse and descent cut out (hole 2 re-anchored AT 13). It asserts that no XY traverse runs below the hop and that the exit is at clearance.\n- `back_to_back_cycle_records_without_a_hop_are_refused_by_name`: the same stream without `RetractPlane`. Every post refuses it with the named message.\n- `a_cycle_read_after_probing_is_seated_at_the_hop`: a section whose first motion is GUARD, TOUCH and a RETREAT to Z1 (below hop Z3), then a cycle at another XY with no rapid to it, then a second hole. Checked from the first known position (`check_from(.., true)`).\n- `the_checker_reads_probe_moves_and_incremental_back_offs`: pins the checker additions:\n  - G31 / G38.2-G38.5 read as straight moves;\n  - G90/G91 incremental back-offs;\n  - the `from_start` watch.\n\n**Revert check:**\n- With #1019's six `.cps` files restored, all three stream tests fail. Fanuc, for example, gives `G00 X30 Y10` traversing at Z1 below the hop Z3, and the no-hop stream posts instead of being refused.\n- With only the `probeSeat()` calls removed, the probe test alone fails (`G73 X30 Y10 ...` moves to the hole at Z-4), so each fix is pinned on its own.\n\n**Goldens.** No generated-stream golden moved: no generator emits these streams. One test-built fixture did:\n- `crates/app/tests/conformance.rs`'s `synth_stream_with` had back-to-back cycle records and no `RetractPlane`, so the hop seat now refuses it.\n- The manager's decision (option 1) is that the fixture now states `PARAM ClearancePlane 10` and `PARAM RetractPlane 5` (R is 2), placed as in the recorded `drill_retract` stream. No leaving rapids were added.\n\nThe six moved goldens were each read line by line:\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/synth_fanuc.nc`, `synth_haas.nc`, `synth_mazak.nc`, `synth_tormach.nc`, `synth_doosan-dnm.nc`, `synth_sinumerik.nc`.\n- Before each hole the tool now climbs to the hop (`G0(0) Z0`, work frame), traverses XY there, and drops to R (`Z-3`). Before, it traversed at R. Nothing else changed apart from Sinumerik's N numbers shifting.\n- `synth_heidenhain.nc` and `synth_carvera.nc` do not move.\n- `WRITE_GOLDEN=1` touched no other file.\n\n### Gates (Linux, on the final head)\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on c12b4d16: **green**. Post suites cover `camcraft-post` lib plus every test binary (`cycle_hop`, `recorded_streams`, all `script_*`, ...). App suites are the full mapped set (the diff includes #1019's shared `inverted_support`), among them posting, conformance, golden_cl, fanuc_post, tormach_post, doosan_dnm_post, probe_dialects, probe_tormach, probe_guard, drill_rplane, drilling_axial, inverted_post and inverted_probe. 2219 passed, 0 failed, 18 ignored, 18.6 min wall.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test conformance -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- The first gate run, before the fixture change, failed only `conformance::the_synthesized_stream_locks_the_tool_and_spindle_words` (the named refusal above).\n\n### Not exercised\n- No real control was run. The posted shapes were read by the checker and by eye for tormach and sinumerik.\n- Doosan's Renishaw Inspection Plus (G65 P9810/P9811) probe path goes through the same `probeSeat()`, but no test runs it with a machine that enables it.\n- Fanuc-lathe face cycles (#1025/#1026) are not covered here.\n\nChangelog: Canned-cycle posts seat a cycle read away from its hole (back-to-back cycle records, or a cycle right after probing) at the section's RetractPlane, or refuse it by name when none is stated (#1028)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0.\n\nFixes #1028\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
